## 1. Purpose

This licence permits the Sgr A* Simulator software to be studied, used, tested, modified and shared for genuine non-commercial purposes while preserving the authorship, provenance and non-commercial status of the original work.

Commercial exploitation of the Software, whether direct or indirect, is not permitted without a separate written commercial licence from the Copyright Holder.

The fact that access to the Software is provided without charge does not, by itself, make a use non-commercial.

## 2. Definitions

For the purposes of this licence:

**“Software”** means the Sgr A* Simulator source code, executable or browser-delivered code, scripts, original user-interface code, original project documentation, configuration files and other original materials distributed with this licence.

**“Copyright Holder”** means Mark Hurrell in relation to original material for which he owns the copyright.

**“You”** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this licence.

**“Modified Work”** means any work containing, modifying, adapting, translating, extending or otherwise deriving from any copyrightable part of the Software.

**“Commercial Use”** means any use that is undertaken for, connected with, intended to obtain, or results in commercial advantage, monetary compensation, revenue, financial return or other material commercial benefit, whether directly or indirectly.

Commercial Use includes use by or on behalf of a commercial organisation where the use contributes to that organisation's activities or interests, even when no separate charge is made for the Software.

**“Non-Commercial Use”** means use undertaken genuinely without direct or indirect commercial purpose, commercial advantage, revenue generation or material financial benefit.

## 3. Permitted Uses

Subject to all conditions of this licence, You may:

a. run and use the Software for personal purposes;

b. study and inspect the source code;

c. use the Software for private experimentation and learning;

d. use the Software for teaching and education where the Software itself is not being commercially exploited;

e. use the Software for genuine non-commercial academic or scientific research;

f. make modifications for permitted non-commercial purposes;

g. create Modified Works for permitted non-commercial purposes;

h. redistribute unmodified copies of the Software without charge;

i. redistribute Modified Works without charge, provided that all requirements of this licence are satisfied.

These permissions apply only to Non-Commercial Use.

## 4. Absolute Commercial-Use Restriction

You may not use, reproduce, modify, distribute, host, provide access to, incorporate, bundle or otherwise exploit the Software or a Modified Work for any Commercial Use without prior written permission from the Copyright Holder.

This prohibition includes, without limitation:

a. selling the Software or a Modified Work;

b. charging for access to the Software or a Modified Work;

c. including the Software in a paid product, package, subscription or service;

d. including the Software in a product or service supported wholly or partly by advertising;

e. distributing or providing the Software through an advertising-supported website, application or platform where the Software contributes to the monetised offering;

f. using the Software to attract users, traffic, customers or subscribers to a monetised service;

g. using the Software in connection with sponsorship, paid promotion, affiliate revenue or other commercial promotional activity;

h. bundling the Software with commercial products or services;

i. using the Software as part of a paid hosting service, software-as-a-service service, cloud service or remotely accessible commercial application;

j. using the Software in connection with consultancy, contract work or paid professional services;

k. using the Software to produce a deliverable supplied as part of paid work;

l. using the Software for commercial research and development;

m. using the Software internally by or for a for-profit business where that use provides or is intended to provide a business, operational, research, development, marketing, financial or competitive benefit;

n. supplying the Software without charge where revenue or commercial benefit is obtained through advertising, sponsorship, subscriptions, associated services, data collection performed for commercial benefit, bundling, promotion or another connected activity;

o. incorporating the Software or a Modified Work into another product whose operation, distribution or availability is commercial in nature.

A price of zero does **not** make an activity non-commercial.

Indirect monetisation is Commercial Use.

An individual who works for a commercial organisation may still use the Software privately in a purely personal capacity, provided that the use is not undertaken for, on behalf of, using the resources of, or for the benefit of that organisation.

## 5. Education and Research

Non-commercial educational institutions, public research bodies, charities and individual researchers may use and modify the Software for genuine non-commercial teaching, study and research.

Research is not considered permitted Non-Commercial Use where the Software is used:

a. primarily for the commercial benefit of a commercial sponsor;

b. to satisfy a commercial development contract;

c. to create proprietary commercial deliverables;

d. to provide exclusive commercial rights, results or advantages to a commercial organisation; or

e. as part of paid commercial research or development.

Publication of ordinary academic research, papers, results, benchmarks and criticism arising from permitted Non-Commercial Use is permitted.

Normal citation and acknowledgement of the Sgr A* Simulator and its original author are encouraged in academic work.

